window.SEARCH_INDEX = [{"u":"docs/getting-started.html","t":"Getting Started","s":"Start Here","h":"","x":"Getting Started Install the mod, then spend your first hour learning the loop that carries you all the way to Void Refinement: gather Qi, sit down, break through."},{"u":"docs/getting-started.html#installation","t":"Installation","s":"Start Here › Getting Started","h":"Getting Started","x":"Client / Singleplayer Drop Cultivation.jar into: %appdata%\\Hytale\\UserData\\Mods\\ Server Drop Cultivation.jar into your server's: mods\\ Delete the old jar first Remove any previous version of Cultivation.jar before adding a new one. Two copies on the classpath will conflict and the server will refuse to boot cleanly. Cultivation works in singleplayer and multiplayer. On a server, only the server needs the jar for the systems to run — but players without it will not see the custom menus."},{"u":"docs/getting-started.html#your-first-hour","t":"Your First Hour","s":"Start Here › Getting Started","h":"Getting Started","x":""},{"u":"docs/getting-started.html#1-turn-on-the-hud","t":"1. Turn on the HUD","s":"Start Here › Getting Started","h":"Getting Started","x":"Run /cultivation hud. You get a persistent corner panel showing your realm, stage, Qi progress and any active ritual progress. You can move it to any of the four corners from /cultivation settings. /cultivation on its own opens the full stats page; /cultivation info prints the same numbers to chat if you would rather not open a menu."},{"u":"docs/getting-started.html#2-earn-your-first-qi","t":"2. Earn your first Qi","s":"Start Here › Getting Started","h":"Getting Started","x":"Two sources, covered in full on Qi Gathering: Kill creatures for a chance at a Spirit, Profound or Divine Core. Right-click a core to absorb it instantly. Meditate with /cultivation meditate to draw ambient Qi out of the chunk you are sitting in. Do both at once Absorbing a core while you are already meditating pays a bonus on top of the core's normal value. Hoard your cores and cash them in during a meditation session."},{"u":"docs/getting-started.html#3-advance-through-the-stages","t":"3. Advance through the stages","s":"Start Here › Getting Started","h":"Getting Started","x":"Sub-stage advancements (Early → Middle → Late → Peak) are short rituals — 8 seconds at the bottom of the ladder — and they need only 200 Qi in the chunk's vein. They happen as soon as you have banked enough Qi and sat down."},{"u":"docs/getting-started.html#4-survive-your-first-breakthrough","t":"4. Survive your first breakthrough","s":"Start Here › Getting Started","h":"Getting Started","x":"Going from Peak of one realm into the next is a different animal. You need a chunk vein holding 750+ Qi, a 24-second uninterrupted ritual, and the nerve to sit still while tribulation lightning comes down on you. Do not stand up Moving away from where you sat down — or cancelling manually — demotes you a sub-stage and wipes your banked Qi. Breakthrough lightning is also genuinely lethal. Go in at full health, and read Realms & Stages before you try."},{"u":"docs/getting-started.html#what-opens-up-next","t":"What Opens Up Next","s":"Start Here › Getting Started","h":"Getting Started","x":"The realm ladder is only the spine. Each of these unlocks as you climb: Unlocks atSystemWhat it gives you Golden Core Races A one-time choice of Human, Demon or Deity, each with its own stat profile Every rank-up Skill Tree Points to spend across nine branches, +1 per advancement and +3 per breakthrough Configurable The Dao An element on the Wu Xing ring, a drifting Yin-Yang balance, and a Devil/Righteous path Any realm Life-Bound Treasures /cultivation bind ties a weapon or armour piece to you so it levels from use Any realm Sects Found a guild, claim a hall on a dragon vein, and eventually go to war over one"},{"u":"docs/getting-started.html#for-server-owners","t":"For Server Owners","s":"Start Here › Getting Started","h":"Getting Started","x":"Every number in the mod lives in a themed JSON config file — nothing is hardcoded — and the ones you are most likely to touch can be edited live in-game through /cultivation admin, with no file editing and no restart. Config Files FileCovers Config.jsonCore Qi curve and per-level stat bonuses SpiritCoreConfig.jsonCore drop chances and Qi values SpiritVeinConfig.jsonSpirit Vein tuning, meditation timing, the talisman BreakthroughConfig.jsonRitual requirements, durations, tribulation toggles LifeBoundConfig.jsonLife-Bound XP curve and combat bonuses RaceSystemConfig.jsonCross-race server behaviour and admin overrides Race/*.jsonEach race's own bonuses and flavour text Config files carry human-readable descriptions next to the less obvious settings."},{"u":"docs/getting-started.html#permissions","t":"Permissions","s":"Start Here › Getting Started","h":"Getting Started","x":"PermissionGrants cultivationThe base command and every player-facing subcommand cultivation.adminAll /cultivation admin subcommands and the admin menu cultivation.debugThe debug command group cultivation.debug.vein/cultivation debug vein Languages Cultivation is fully localised in English and Simplified Chinese (with proper Xianxia terminology throughout), plus partial translations for Portuguese (Brazil), Russian and Ukrainian."},{"u":"docs/qi-gathering.html","t":"Qi Gathering","s":"The Path","h":"","x":"Qi Gathering Qi is the currency of the whole mod — it buys every advancement and every breakthrough. There are two ways to earn it, and they are deliberately better together than apart."},{"u":"docs/qi-gathering.html#meditation-spirit-veins","t":"Meditation & Spirit Veins","s":"The Path › Qi Gathering","h":"Qi Gathering","x":"/cultivation meditate sits your character cross-legged and slowly draws ambient energy from the Spirit Vein of the chunk you are standing in. A Spirit Vein is a real per-chunk energy pool: it has a capacity, it depletes as you draw from it, and it regenerates over time. Camp on one chunk long enough and it will run dry, and your Qi-per-second falls with it until it recovers. Move around Because veins deplete locally and regenerate on their own clock, the fastest way to gather is to rotate between a few good chunks rather than sit on one forever. Use /cultivation debug vein to read the current chunk's remaining Qi."},{"u":"docs/qi-gathering.html#vein-tiers","t":"Vein Tiers","s":"The Path › Qi Gathering","h":"Qi Gathering","x":"Not every chunk is equal. Most are ordinary, but some roll richer, and a rare few sit on a dragon vein — the chunks worth fighting a sect war over. Common Vein The baseline. Regenerates at the standard rate. Rich Vein A noticeably faster regeneration multiplier — worth returning to. Dragon Vein The best land in the world. Sect halls and cave abodes are claimed on these. Server owners: the drain rule A vein's regeneration multiplied by its tier bonus must stay below the meditation drain rate. If regen × multiplier ever exceeds drain, that chunk becomes an infinite Qi fountain and the entire progression curve stops mattering."},{"u":"docs/qi-gathering.html#the-qi-gathering-talisman","t":"The Qi Gathering Talisman","s":"The Path › Qi Gathering","h":"Qi Gathering","x":"Hold a Qi Gathering Talisman anywhere in your hotbar while meditating and your Spirit Vein absorption rate goes up. It does not need to be in your hand — carrying it is enough. Rate and behaviour are set in SpiritVeinConfig.json."},{"u":"docs/qi-gathering.html#cultivation-cores","t":"Cultivation Cores","s":"The Path › Qi Gathering","h":"Qi Gathering","x":"Killing creatures has a chance to drop a cultivation core. Right-click one to absorb it for an instant chunk of Qi — no meditation required, which makes cores the answer when you want to progress while doing something else. CoreRarityRole Spirit Core Common The everyday drop. Small, steady Qi. Profound Core Uncommon A meaningful jump — worth saving for a ritual. Divine Core Rare Large enough to carry a stubborn breakthrough on its own. Stack the two sources Absorbing a core while you are already meditating grants a bonus on top of the core's normal Qi value. Save your cores for a meditation session rather than absorbing them on sight. Drop chances and Qi values for all three cores live in SpiritCoreConfig.json."},{"u":"docs/qi-gathering.html#weather-resonance","t":"Weather Resonance","s":"The Path › Qi Gathering","h":"Qi Gathering","x":"The sky matters. Meditating during active weather grants a Qi multiplier, and the multiplier is larger when the weather matches the element of the Dao you walk. ConditionMultiplier Weather matching your chosen dao element×1.5 Any other active weather×1.15 Clear skies×1.0 Which weather maps to which element is itself configurable, by keyword, in DaoConfig.json — so a server using custom weather assets can wire them in without any code."},{"u":"docs/qi-gathering.html#putting-it-together","t":"Putting It Together","s":"The Path › Qi Gathering","h":"Qi Gathering","x":"An efficient early loop looks like this: Hunt until you have a handful of cores and a Qi Gathering Talisman. Find a rich chunk with /cultivation debug vein and sit down. Meditate through the weather if there is any — rain pays better than clear sky. Absorb your saved cores during the session for the stacking bonus. When the vein thins out, move a few chunks over and repeat. Related Config FileCovers SpiritVeinConfig.jsonVein capacity, regeneration, tiers, meditation timing, talisman SpiritCoreConfig.jsonCore drop chances and Qi values DaoConfig.jsonWeather → element keyword mapping and resonance multipliers Config.jsonThe Qi curve every one of these feeds into"},{"u":"docs/realms.html","t":"Realms & Stages","s":"The Path","h":"","x":"Realms & Stages Every player starts at Body Refinement, Early-Stage and climbs toward immortality through seven realms, each split into four sub-stages: Early, Middle, Late and Peak. Twenty-eight rungs in all."},{"u":"docs/realms.html#the-ladder","t":"The Ladder","s":"The Path › Realms & Stages","h":"Realms & Stages","x":"Within each realm you advance Early → Middle → Late → Peak, then break through into the next realm's Early-Stage. Higher realms and stages grant additive max health and a percentage damage bonus, both tuned in Config.json. 體 Body Refinement Tempering flesh and sinew before a single wisp of energy will hold. REALM I 氣 Qi Condensation Ambient spirit energy finally gathers and stays inside the body. REALM II 築 Foundation Establishment The base is laid. From here the climb is steep but no longer fragile. REALM III 丹 Golden Core Formation A core forms in the dantian — and your one-time race choice unlocks. REALM IV 嬰 Nascent Soul The soul takes an infant form and can act briefly apart from the body. REALM V 神 Soul Formation Soul and body fuse into something the mortal world no longer recognises. REALM VI 虛 Void Refinement The last realm the mod ships — and the last one the world can hold. REALM VII"},{"u":"docs/realms.html#advancements-vs-breakthroughs","t":"Advancements vs. Breakthroughs","s":"The Path › Realms & Stages","h":"Realms & Stages","x":"Both are real, timed meditation rituals. Bank enough Qi, sit down in a chunk whose Spirit Vein holds enough energy, and the ritual progresses for as long as you keep meditating. The chunk-Qi requirement is a presence check, not a drain — the vein is not consumed by the ritual — but a vein that falls below the bar will pause the ritual until it regenerates. Sub-Stage AdvancementRealm Breakthrough When Early → Middle → Late → Peak Peak → next realm's Early-Stage Minimum chunk Qi 200 Advancement-Min-Chunk-Qi 750 Breakthrough-Min-Chunk-Qi Base duration 8s Advancement-Base-Seconds 24s Breakthrough-Base-Seconds Duration scaling ×1.3 per realm reached ×1.35 per realm reached Tribulation lightning off by default on, and lethal Skill points +1 Points-Per-Advancement +1, plus 2 more Points-Per-Breakthrough Failure costs you Cancelling a ritual — by drifting away from where you sat down, or by standing up manually — demotes you one sub-stage, wipes your banked Qi, and revokes the skill points that stage originally granted. You are never demoted below Early-Stage of your current realm, so a failed breakthrough can never cost you a whole realm."},{"u":"docs/realms.html#ritual-flow","t":"Ritual Flow","s":"The Path › Realms & Stages","h":"Realms & Stages","x":"The heavens are watching Breakthrough lightning is genuinely lethal — it can kill you outright at low health. A cultivator who has leaned far enough into Yin or Yang faces the Heart-Devil Trial instead, which tests composure rather than hit points. Both are tunable, and advancement tribulations are off by default."},{"u":"docs/realms.html#tuning-the-curve","t":"Tuning the Curve","s":"The Path › Realms & Stages","h":"Realms & Stages","x":"Nothing here is hardcoded. The realm/stage curve and its stat rewards live in Config.json; the ritual requirements above live in BreakthroughConfig.json. Both can be edited live in-game through /cultivation admin without touching a file or restarting the server. Related Commands CommandDoes /cultivationOpen the stats page — realm, stage, Qi progress /cultivation infoPrint the same readout to chat /cultivation meditateBegin the ritual (alias /cultivation cultivate) /cultivation admin setrealm <player> <realm>Set a realm directly admin /cultivation admin setstage <player> <stage>Set a sub-stage directly admin"},{"u":"index.html#the-path-at-a-glance","t":"The Path at a Glance","s":"Start Here › Cultivation","h":"Cultivation","x":"Every cultivator walks the same opening road — gather Qi, climb the realms, endure the tribulation — and then chooses how to spend the power that road grants them."},{"u":"index.html#systems","t":"Systems","s":"Start Here › Cultivation","h":"Cultivation","x":"Cultivation is built as a stack of independent systems. You can run only the realm ladder, or turn on every one of these."},{"u":"index.html#realms-stages","t":"Realms & Stages","s":"Start Here › Cultivation","h":"Cultivation","x":"Seven realms, four sub-stages each. Advancement is routine; breakthrough is a ritual you can fail."},{"u":"index.html#qi-gathering","t":"Qi Gathering","s":"Start Here › Cultivation","h":"Cultivation","x":"Meditate to drain a chunk's Spirit Vein, or hunt creatures for Spirit, Profound and Divine Cores."},{"u":"index.html#tribulations","t":"Tribulations","s":"Start Here › Cultivation","h":"Cultivation","x":"Lightning falls on every breakthrough. Lean too far into Yin or Yang and you face the Heart-Devil Trial instead."},{"u":"index.html#the-dao","t":"The Dao","s":"Start Here › Cultivation","h":"Cultivation","x":"Ten elemental daos on a Wu Xing counter-ring, a drifting Yin-Yang balance, and a Devil/Righteous path split."},{"u":"index.html#techniques","t":"Techniques","s":"Start Here › Cultivation","h":"Cultivation","x":"Active arts learned from lootable manuals — fly on your sword, cross a valley in one step, call down a thunder palm."},{"u":"index.html#sects-war","t":"Sects & War","s":"Start Here › Cultivation","h":"Cultivation","x":"Found a sect, claim a hall on a dragon vein, raise formations, and take a rival's mountain by siege."},{"u":"index.html#alchemy","t":"Alchemy","s":"Start Here › Cultivation","h":"Cultivation","x":"Brew pills that steady a ritual, ward off the inner demon, or push a stubborn breakthrough over the line."},{"u":"index.html#spirit-beasts","t":"Spirit Beasts","s":"Start Here › Cultivation","h":"Cultivation","x":"Tame or hatch companions that cultivate their own realm beside you as Guardian, Gatherer or Warden."},{"u":"index.html#public-api","t":"Public API","s":"Start Here › Cultivation","h":"Cultivation","x":"Roughly 135 cancellable events, open registries, and a provider hook that lets a mod replace the ladder entirely. Sample pages only This wiki is being built out. Cards without a link, and sidebar rows marked soon, are systems that exist in the mod but do not have their page written yet."},{"u":"index.html#the-seven-realms","t":"The Seven Realms","s":"Start Here › Cultivation","h":"Cultivation","x":"Every player starts at Body Refinement, Early-Stage. Each realm grants additive max health and a percentage damage bonus, so the gap between a mortal and a Void Refiner is enormous. 體 Body RefinementWhere every mortal begins — tempering flesh before energy. REALM I 氣 Qi CondensationAmbient spirit energy first gathers and holds inside the body. REALM II 築 Foundation EstablishmentThe base is laid; progress stops being reversible by accident. REALM III 丹 Golden Core FormationA core forms. Your race may be chosen here, once. REALM IV 嬰 Nascent SoulThe soul takes an infant form and can act apart from the body. REALM V 神 Soul FormationSoul and body fuse into something no longer quite human. REALM VI 虛 Void RefinementThe last realm before the mortal world stops being enough. REALM VII Full realm mechanics →"},{"u":"index.html#start-here","t":"Start Here","s":"Start Here › Cultivation","h":"Cultivation","x":""},{"u":"index.html#installation-first-steps","t":"Installation & First Steps","s":"Start Here › Cultivation","h":"Cultivation","x":"Get the jar in the right folder, then your first hour: meditate, absorb a core, and reach Qi Condensation."},{"u":"index.html#how-qi-actually-works","t":"How Qi Actually Works","s":"Start Here › Cultivation","h":"Cultivation","x":"Spirit Veins, vein tiers, the talisman, core drop rates, and why over-farming one chunk stops paying. Quick Reference CommandDoes /cultivationOpen your cultivation stats page /cultivation meditateSit and draw Qi from the chunk's Spirit Vein /cultivation hudToggle the persistent corner HUD /cultivation raceOpen the race menu (Golden Core Formation and up) /cultivation adminLive in-game config editor admin Aliases: /cult and /qi both work anywhere /cultivation does."}];
